; Map value-equality is order-INDEPENDENT: two maps with the same key/value
; pairs are `=` regardless of insertion order. Holds on the EIR VM (oracle) and
; the interpreter.
; expect-fail: wasm — wasm codegen has no structural `=` for compound values; it
;   compares maps (and vectors) by reference, so `[= {:a 1} {:a 1}]` is already
;   false there. Order-independent map equality is a VM/interp guarantee until
;   wasm grows a deep `=`. Retire this annotation when it does.
[fn main []
  [println [= {:a 1 :b 2} {:b 2 :a 1}]]   ; true  — same pairs, diff order
  [println [= {:a 1 :b 2} {:a 1 :b 3}]]]  ; false — :b differs
